# Game type dumps are ~26 MB of pretty-printed JSON (about 2.7 MB compressed in git).
# They are tracked deliberately: a dump can only be captured from a *running* client, so
# once a patch ships there is no way back to the previous version's layout. The checked-in
# dumps are the only record of what the offsets were when our code last worked.
#
# Suppress textual diffing: a line-by-line diff of two 26 MB dumps is unreadable noise.
# Compare them with the tool that understands the structure instead:
#     uv run python tools/typedump.py diff <old.json> <new.json>
tools/r*_WizardDev.json -diff

# A released template version is checked against the SHA-256 Release recorded for its
# bytes, and a draft must round-trip byte for byte, so nothing under templates/ may have
# its line endings rewritten on checkout (core.autocrlf would turn them into CRLF).
templates/** -text
